  "solution": "**Given**\n\n x⁴ + (1)/(x⁴) = 142\n\n**Formula used**\n\n(x + 1/x)² = x² + 1/x² + 2\n\nx3 + 1/x3 = (x + 1/x)³ - 3(x + 1/x)\n\n**Calculation**\n\n⇒ x4 + 1/x4 + 2 = (x² + 1/x²)2\n\n⇒ 142 + 2 = (x2 + 1/x2)2\n\n⇒ (x2 + 1/x 2) = √144 = 12\n\n⇒ (x + 1/x)2 = x2 + 1/x2 + 2\n\n⇒ (x + 1/x)2 = 12 + 2\n\n⇒ (x + 1/x) = √14\n\n⇒ x3 + 1/x3 = (x + 1/x)3 - 3(x + 1/x) \n\n= (√14)3 - 3(√14)\n\n= 14√14 - 3√14 = 11√14\n\n(x⁷ + 1/x⁷) = (x4 + 1/x⁴) × (x³ + 1/x³) - (x + 1/x)\n\n= 142 × 11√14 - √14\n\n= 1562√14 - √14\n\n= √14 (1562 - 1)\n\n= 1561√14\n\n**The answer is 1561√14**",
